    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="1713" n="1562" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v07-09mSupp/pg1562"/>

                <head>365. Memorandum from President Kennedy to Martin, October 14<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d365-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1963-10-14">October 14, 1963</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d365-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d365-1"/>
                <p>I am asking the Secretary of the Treasury to form a Committee to review the
                    United States position in the discussions now in progress on the evolution of
                    the international monetary system.</p>
                <p>The Committee is described in the attached memorandum. I would appreciate it if
                    you would be willing to sit with the Committee when it meets.</p>
                <closer><signed corresp="#p_KJF_1">John Kennedy</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d365-a1.xml" xpointer="d365-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d365-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d365-f1-content">
                <p>Martin’s participation in meetings to review U.S. position on evolution of
                    international monetary system. Confidential. 2 pp. Kennedy Library, National
                    Security Files, Subjects Series, Balance of Payments and Gold, 10/63–11/63, Box
                    292.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
